course: dictionary
lesson: 11400
title: Accompany: going along with someone or something
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: To accompany someone is to go somewhere with them. «Children must be accompanied by an adult at the swimming pool.» The word accompanied tells you a grown-up has to go along too, not just stand at the gate.
explain: Accompany can also mean to come or happen with something. «Gravy usually accompanies roast beef.» Gravy is served together with the beef, so accompany means come with. You can check this by swapping in «comes with»: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In music, to accompany a singer or player is to play alongside them. «The pianist accompanied the choir» means the piano played the tune while the choir sang. The pianist is not the star, but the music does not work without them.
fact: Accompany means to go with someone, to come with something, or to play music alongside someone.
fact: «Accompanied» and «accompanying» are other forms of the same word.
fact: «Accompanied by» means with someone or something else, as in «She was accompanied by her dog».
fact: Clues in the sentence often show the meaning: a walk, a meal, or a song all show what accompany means.
fact: A useful check is to swap in «go with» or «come with». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «The little boy must be accompanied by an adult at the pool.» What does accompanied mean here? | Left alone at the side of the pool | * Gone along with someone to keep them safe | Shouted at by a grown-up | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The pianist will accompany the choir.» What does accompany mean? | Sing louder than them | * Play music alongside them | Ask them to leave the room | Stop them from singing
exercise: «Gravy usually accompanies roast beef.» What does accompanies mean? | Is cooked before | Costs more than | Runs away from | * Comes with
test: «Mum will accompany me to the dentist.» What does accompany mean? | Send me a letter about the dentist | Take a photo of me | * Go along with me | Wait for me at home
test: «The singer was accompanied by a guitar.» What does accompanied by mean? | Chased away by a guitar | * Played alongside, with a guitar | Replaced by a guitar | Hidden under a guitar
exam: Which meaning best fits accompany? | Forget about someone | * Go with someone, or come with something | Shout at someone | Break something into pieces
